2. GADS (https://github.com/shamanec/GADS), read at tag v6.0.0
--------------------------------------------------------------

GADS has two licences. Its LICENSE-OVERVIEW.txt says:

    "Except as noted below, all files in this repository are licensed under
     the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0."
    "The following components are proprietary and licensed under the GADS
     Proprietary License: - hub-ui"

* LICENSE in the GADS repository is the AGPL-3.0 text.
* PROPRIETARY-LICENSE.txt ("GADS PROPRIETARY LICENSE", last updated
  23/MAY/2025) covers hub-ui, the hub's web interface. It grants "a
  non-exclusive, non-transferable, limited license to use the proprietary
  components of GADS ... solely for your internal business purposes" and
  forbids, among other things, to "copy, modify, ... decompile, disassemble,
  or reverse engineer" it and to "distribute, sublicense, lease, rent, loan,
  or otherwise transfer the Proprietary Software to any third party".
* hub-ui is a git submodule that points at a private repository; its source
  is not public. Upstream's release binaries embed a built, obfuscated copy.

What this kit does with each part:

a) The hub. install.ps1 downloads the publisher's own release file
   (gads-win.zip of v6.0.0) directly from the publisher's GitHub release page
   to the farm computer, and verifies its SHA-256. This repository and its
   releases do not contain, mirror or modify that file. The person running a
   farm uses it on their own computer for their own business; whether that
   use fits the proprietary licence of the embedded hub-ui is for that person
   to judge from the licence text quoted above.

b) The provider. The release assets of this repository include
   GADS-drag.exe, built by .github/workflows/build-gads.yml from the AGPL-3.0
   source of GADS at the pinned commit plus patch/provider-drag.patch.
   - It is built WITHOUT the "ui" build tag, so it contains no hub-ui code.
     (In GADS, embed_ui.go embeds hub-ui/build only under that tag;
     no_embed_ui.go is used otherwise.)
   - It is distributed under AGPL-3.0. The complete corresponding source
     (the patched tree, including the generated docs package) is attached to
     the same release as GADS-drag-<version>-source.tar.gz.
   - Like every GADS binary, it embeds the "resources" directory of the GADS
     repository: gads-broadcast.ipa and gads-settings.apk (GADS's own helper
     apps), three zsign executables (https://github.com/zhlynn/zsign), and an
     iOS developer disk image with its manifest and trust cache
     (resources/ios-ddi). GADS's LICENSE-OVERVIEW.txt places all files other
     than hub-ui under AGPL-3.0; this kit relies on that statement and has
     not examined the origin of those files further. In particular, the
     developer disk image is Apple software as far as we can tell. Whoever
     publishes releases of this repository should take their own view on
     redistributing a binary that embeds it, exactly as upstream's releases
     do. An alternative that redistributes nothing is to build the provider
     on each farm computer from upstream source.

c) AGPL-3.0, section 13 (remote network interaction). A farm operator who
   runs the modified provider and lets users interact with it over a network
   must offer those users its source. The source is public: this repository
   (the patch), upstream at the pinned commit, and the source archive on the
   release. Operators who change the provider further must publish their
   changes in the same way.

