versions pinned in versions.json. Licences as stated by the projects:

* MongoDB Community Server (MongoDB.Server) - Server Side Public License v1
* MongoDB Database Tools (MongoDB.DatabaseTools) - Apache License 2.0
* Node.js (OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS) - MIT and bundled third-party licences
* FFmpeg, "full" build by Gyan (Gyan.FFmpeg) - GPL v3 for that build
* cloudflared (Cloudflare.cloudflared) - Apache License 2.0; use of the
  Cloudflare service is under Cloudflare's terms
* NSSM (NSSM.NSSM) - public domain; the installer keeps a private copy of
  nssm.exe in C:\farm\bin on the farm computer

Only with "install.ps1 -WithAppium", installed with npm from the npm registry:

* Appium (appium) and its iOS driver (appium-xcuitest-driver) - Apache
  License 2.0. The GADS provider then installs its own Appium plugin
  (appium-gads, part of GADS) by itself.

Not installed by the kit, but required for iPhones (docs/phones.md):

* Apple Devices or iTunes (Apple) - Apple's licence terms
* WebDriverAgent, fork by the GADS author
  (https://github.com/shamanec/WebDriverAgent) - BSD licence of
  WebDriverAgent. The farm operator downloads the pre-built file from that
  repository's own release page and signs it with their own Apple Developer
